<title>JAPAN: Japan Sept construction orders rise 59.4 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Sept construction orders rise 59.4 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's construction orders in September rose 59.4 percent from a year earlier to 3.65 trillion yen, the Construction Ministry said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (in billions of yen unless specified, with year-on-year changes):</p>
<p> Domestic private-sector orders		2,444.38  +91.3</p>
<p> Domestic public-sector orders		   953.86  +23.0</p>
<p> Foreign government facilities in Japan and</p>
<p>    orders of less than 10 million yen	  56.27   +3.1</p>
<p> Orders received abroad			    196.74   +7.4</p>
<p> Total						3.65 trln  +59.4</p>
</text>
